# Qwen

Qwen is a family of large language models developed by Alibaba Cloud AI. Qwen is designed to be versatile and easy-to-use, with efficient inference experience. Qwen has been trained on a massive amount of data and has a rich set of capabilities, supporting a wide range of tasks such as text generation, question-answering, and more. It is available for both online and offline use, and can be easily integrated into various applications, including chatbots, virtual assistants, and more.

## Features

- **High-Accuracy Models**: Qwen models are based on large-scale pre-training, with a high degree of accuracy and generalization ability.

- **Efficient Computing**: Qwen models are optimized for efficient computing, with faster inference speed and lower latency.

- **Easy-to-Use**: Qwen models are easy to use, with simple API interfaces and easy integration into applications.

- **Rich Capabilities**: Qwen models support a wide range of capabilities, including text generation, question-answering, and more.

## Online Use

Qwen models are available online at [Qwen online](https://qwen.zhuanzhuan.com/), where you can interact with the model in real-time and test its performance.

## Offline Use

Qwen models can also be used offline. You can download pre-trained models from the [Qwen model hub](https://qwen.zhuanzhuan.com/model), and use them in your own applications. The Qwen model hub provides a variety of models with different sizes and capabilities, to meet the different needs of users.

## Integration

Qwen models can be easily integrated into various applications, such as chatbots, virtual assistants, and more. The Qwen SDK provides a simple API interface for easy integration, and can be easily integrated into any programming language or framework. The Qwen SDK also supports online and offline use, with different SDKs available for different platforms.

## Documentation

The documentation for Qwen models and the Qwen SDK can be found at [Qwen documentation](https://qwen.zhuanzhuan.com/doc).

## License

Qwen models are available under the [Apache License 2.0](https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0).

## Contact

If you have any questions or suggestions, you can contact us at [Qwen support](https://qwen.zhuanzhuan.com/support).
