# Sentinel

[![GoDoc](https://godoc.org/github.com/zhiyueyue/sentinel?status.svg)](https://godoc.org/github.com/zhiyueyue/sentinel)

Sentinel is a rate limiter, it has two parts, one is the manager and the other is the limiter. The manager is responsible for managing the limiter, the limiter is responsible for executing the limiting logic. The limiter can be a memory based limiter, or a database based limiter.

[Chinese Doc](https://github.com/zhiyueyue/sentinel/blob/master/README_cn.md)

## Memory Limiter

Memory limiter is the most simple and easiest to use, it is a single point rate limiter. The following is an example of using memory limiter:

```go
// Create a memory limiter.
limiter, err := sentinel.NewMemLimiter(10)

// Create a manager with memory limiter.
manager := sentinel.NewManager(limiter)

// Add a limiter to the manager.
manager.Add("limiter1")

// If you need to remove the limiter, you can call the following function.
// manager.Remove("limiter1")

// Get the limiter and use it.
limiter1 := manager.Get("limiter1")
limiter1.Limit()
```

## Database Limiter

Database based limiter is a multi-point rate limiter, it can be used to share the limiter among multiple instances. The following is an example of using database based limiter:

```go
// Create a database based limiter.
// The database based limiter needs to be initialized before use, and it needs to be connected to the database.
