# Qwen-Chat
Qwen is a large language model created by Alibaba Cloud. This repository contains a chat interface for interacting with Qwen in a web browser.

## Installation
To install Qwen-Chat, you will need to have Node.js and npm installed on your machine. Then, you can clone this repository and run the following commands:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/alibaba/Qwen-Chat.git
cd Qwen-Chat
npm install
npm run start
```

This will start a local server at `localhost:8080`, where you can access Qwen-Chat in your browser.

## Usage
Once you have installed Qwen-Chat, you can start chatting with Qwen by typing your messages in the chat window. Qwen will respond with its own messages, which will be displayed below your input.

You can also use the following commands to control Qwen:

- `/clear`: Clears the chat window.
- `/help`: Displays a list of available commands.
- `/reset`: Resets the chat window and clears the conversation history.

To use these commands, simply type the command followed by a space and then press enter.

## Configuration
You can configure Qwen-Chat by editing the `config.json` file in the root directory of the project. This file contains the following options:

- `apiKey`: Your Al<|fim_suffix|>hat is hosted on Alibaba Cloud.

You can find more information about Qwen at the [Qwen website](https://qwen.alibabatech.com/).

## License
This project is licensed under the MIT License. See the LICENSE file for more information.
<|fim_middle|>ibaba Cloud API key.
- `model`: The model to use for generating responses. Currently, only the `qwen-7b` model is supported.
- `temperature`: The temperature to use for generating responses. This value controls the randomness of the responses. A higher temperature value will result in more random responses, while a lower temperature value will result in more deterministic responses.
- `topP`: The top-p value to use for generating responses. This value controls the diversity of the responses. A higher top-p value will result in more diverse responses, while a lower top-p value will result in more focused responses.

## Limitations
Qwen-Chat is a basic interface for interacting with Qwen and is not intended to be a production-level service. As such, it has the following limitations:

- Qwen-Chat only supports the `qwen-7b` model, which is not the most performant model available.
- Qwen-Chat does not support multi-turn conversations.
- Qwen-Chat does not support fine-tuning.

## Acknowledgements
Qwen-Chat is based on the [Qwen JavaScript SDK](https://github.com/alibaba/Qwen-JS-SDK) created by Alibaba Cloud. It uses [Socket.io](https://socket.io/) for real-time communication and [taiji](https://github.com/alibaba/taiji) for the UI.

Qwen is developed by Alibaba Cloud and is available for free at [Qwen.alibabatech.com](https://qwen.alibabatech.com/). It is a large language model t<|file_sep|><|fim_prefix|>/src/components/Chat/Chat.js
import React, { useEffect, useRef, useState } from 'react';
import { useChat } from '@/hooks/useChat';
import { ClearIcon, MicIcon, SendIcon } from '@/components/Icons';
import { useMicrophone } from '@/hooks/useMicrophone';
import { ChatMessage } from './ChatMessage';
import { ChatInput } from './ChatInput';
import { useTranslation } from 'react-i18next';
import { AutoChat } from './AutoChat';
import { useSystem } from '@/hooks/useSystem';

export const Chat = () => {
  const { t } = useTranslation();
  const { system } = useSystem();
  const { messages, isSubmitting, onSubmit, onSubmitEnter } = useChat();
  const [isAutoChatting, setIsAutoChatting] = useState(false);
  const [isClearChat, setIsClearChat] = useState(false);
  const ref = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);
  const { isListening, start, stop } = useMicrophone();
  const handleAutoChat = () => {
    setIsAutoChatting(true);
    setIsClearChat(false);
  };
  const handleClear = () => {
    setIsAutoChatting(false);
    setIsClearChat(true);
  };
  useEffect(() => {
    if (isClearChat) {
      ref.current?.scrollTo({ top: 0, behavior: 'smooth' });
      setIsClearChat(false);
    }
  }, [messages, isClearChat]);
  return (
    <div className="mx-auto my-auto flex h-[calc(100vh-70px)] w-full max-w-4xl flex-col justify-between bg-white ">
      <div className="flex h-full w-full flex-col overflow-y-auto">
        {system && <ChatMessage message={system} />}
        {messages &&
          messages.map((item, index) => {
            return (
              <ChatMessage key={index} message={item} isLast={index === messages.length - 1} />
            );
          })}
        {isAutoChatting && (
          <AutoChat
            isAutoChatting={isAutoChatting}
            setIsAutoChatting={setIsAutoChatting}
            isSubmitting={isSubmitting}
            onSubmit={onSubmit}
            onSubmitEnter={onSubmitEnter}
          />
        )}
      </div>
      <div className="flex h-auto w-full flex-row items-center justify-between border-t border-slate-200 px-4 py-3 ">
        <div className="flex w-full gap-3">
          <div className="flex flex-row gap-2">
            <button
              className="flex h-[32px] w-[32px] items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-slate-200 hover:bg-slate-300"
              onClick={handleClear}
            >
              <ClearIcon />
            </button>
            <div className="flex h-[32px] w-[32px] items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-slate-200 hover:bg-slate-300">
              <MicIcon className={isListening ? 'text-red-500' : ''} />
            </div>
            <button
              className="flex h-[32px] w-[32px] items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-slate-200 hover:bg-slate-300"
              onClick={handleAutoChat}
            >
              <SendIcon />
            </button>
          </div>
          <div className="flex h-[64px] w-[60%] rounded-2xl bg-slate-200 px-4">
            <input
              className="h-full w-full rounded-2xl bg-slate-200 text-sm"
              onKeyPress={(e) => {
                if (e.key === 'Enter') {
                  onSubmitEnter();
                }
              }}
              ref={ref}
              disabled={isAutoChatting}
              onKeyDown={(e) => {
                if (e.key === 'Enter') {
                  e.preventDefault();
                }
              }}
            />
          </div>
        </div>
        <div className="flex flex-row gap-2">
          <button
            className={`flex h-[32px] w-[32px] items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-slate-200 hover:bg-slate-300`}
            onClick={() => {
              isListening ? stop() : start();
            }}
          >
            {isListening ? (
              <div className="flex h-[24px] w-[24px] items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-red-500 text-white">
                STOP
              </div>
            ) : (
              <MicIcon />
            )}
          </button>
          <button
            className="flex h-[32px] w-[32px] items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-slate-200 hover:bg-slate-300"
            onClick={() => {
              console.log('send');
            }}
          >
            <SendIcon />
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  );
};

