# Qwen

Qwen is an open-source AI assistant that is built using React, TypeScript, and Redux. It was created by [Alibaba Cloud](https://www.alibabacloud.com/), a cloud computing company in China. 

## Features

- Real-time chat with AI assistant
- Natural language processing and understanding
- Support for multiple languages
- Easy to use and customize

## Getting Started

To get started with Qwen, you need to have Node.js and npm installed on your computer. You can download them from [here](https://nodejs.org/en/download/).

Once you have Node.js and npm installed, you can clone this repository and run the following commands:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/AlibabaCloud/qwen.git
cd qwen
npm install
npm start
```

This will start a local development server at `http://localhost:3000`.

## Contributing

We welcome contributions from the community. If you would like to contribute to Qwen, please follow these steps:

1. Fork the repository
2. Create a new branch for your feature or bug fix
3. Make your changes and commit them
4. Push your branch to your fork
5. Submit a pull request to the main repository

## License

Qwen is licensed under the [Apache License 2.0](https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0.html).<|file_sep|><|fim_prefix|>/webapp/src/app/store/selectors.ts
