# Qwen C++ Server
This folder contains the interface for the Qwen C++ server.
The Qwen C++ server is based on [Qwen C++ Inference](https://github.com/QwenLM/Qwen-Inference).

## Build
First, install the Qwen C++ Inference library in the folder `Qwen-Inference`. Then, build the server:
```sh
cd qwen_cpp_server
mkdir build
cd build
cmake ..
make
```
## Usage
The server can be started by:
```sh
./qwen_cpp_server 0.0.0.0 8080
```
The server can be stopped by sending a SIGTERM signal to the process.

## API
The server provides the following API:
- `POST /generate`
  - `text`: The text to generate from.
  - `max_tokens`: The maximum number of tokens to generate.
  - `top_p`: The top_p sampling parameter.
  - `top_k`: The top_k sampling parameter.
  - `temperature`: The temperature sampling parameter.

## Examples
Change the `URL` variable in the examples to the url of the server.
### Python
```python
import requests

URL = "http://0.0.0.0:8080/generate"

def generate(text, max_tokens=100, top_p=0.9, top_k=0, temperature=0.8):
    response = requests.post(URL, json={
        "text": text,
        "max_tokens": max_tokens,
        "top_p": top_p,
        "top_k": top_k,
        "temperature": temperature,
    })
    return response.json()["text"]

print(generate("Once upon a time,"))
```
### C++
```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <string>
#include <curl/curl.h>

class CurlWrapper {
public:
    CurlWrapper() {
        curl = curl_easy_init();
    }

    ~CurlWrapper() {
        curl_easy_cleanup(curl);
    }

    void set_option(CURLoption option, long value) {
        curl_easy_setopt(curl, option, value);
    }

    void perform() {
        curl_easy_perform(curl);
    }

    std::string get_response() {
        curl_easy_getinfo(curl, CURLINFO_RESPONSE_CODE, &response_code);
        if (response_code != 200) {
            return "";
        }
        return std::string(response, strlen(response));
    }

private:
    CURL* curl;
    char response[1024];
    long response_code;
};

int main() {
    CurlWrapper curl;
    curl.set_option(CURLOPT_URL, "http://0.0.0.0:8080/generate");
    curl.set_option(CURLOPT_POST, 1);
    curl.set_option(CURLOPT_POSTFIELDS, "{\"text\": \"Once upon a time,\"}");
    curl.set_option(CURLOPT_WRITEFUNCTION, [](void* buffer, size_t size, size_t nmemb, void* userp) {
        std::string* response = static_cast<std::string*>(userp);
        response->append(static_cast<char*>(buffer), size * nmemb);
        return size * nmemb;
    });
    curl.set_option(CURLOPT_WRITEDATA, &response);
    curl.perform();
    std::cout << response << std::endl;
}
